window.FIELD_CHAPTER_PARTS["book-2-full-book"][24] = "<h1>PART 23: FIVE END-TO-END PRODUCT JOURNEYS</h1>\n<h2>23.0 What this section is and how to use it</h2>\n<p>The next five chapters take you through complete product builds — from initial idea to launched product to post-launch retrospective. Each is a master class disguised as a case study.</p>\n<p>For each journey, you'll see:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>How the problem was identified.</li>\n<li>How discovery played out (what we asked, what we learned, what surprised us).</li>\n<li>The full PRD as it would actually be written.</li>\n<li>AI architecture decisions with explicit trade-offs.</li>\n<li>The metrics tree.</li>\n<li>The MVP plan with kill criteria.</li>\n<li>The trade-offs we made and why.</li>\n<li>The post-launch retrospective (real-feeling, including failures).</li>\n<li>A &quot;What would Google look for here?&quot; section that translates the build into APM-interview-relevant signals.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Read these slowly. The patterns recur across product types. Five different domains, but the underlying PM craft is the same.</p>\n<p>The five journeys, with rationale for inclusion:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Saarthi</strong> — Consumer AI study companion for JEE/NEET aspirants. Tests: AI PM, consumer, Indian context, regulated-by-society category (education).</li>\n<li><strong>ClearOps</strong> — B2B SaaS ops platform for Indian D2C brands. Tests: B2B, integrations, multi-stakeholder dynamics.</li>\n<li><strong>Mentora</strong> — Tutor marketplace for Class 9-12 students. Tests: marketplace dynamics, cold start, trust.</li>\n<li><strong>Vega</strong> — Internal AI eval platform inside a hypothetical fintech. Tests: platform PM, internal customers, deprecation.</li>\n<li><strong>Karya</strong> — Autonomous email/calendar agent for knowledge workers. Tests: agentic AI, autonomy UX, the hardest of the five.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Total length: ~50,000 words across five journeys. Not because the brief asked for length but because each requires that depth to be complete.</p>\n<hr>\n";
